### This like a simple test client (Browser)
### Three Hash to start new call
### This is to test Hello World Service
http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/MyService/anshul(name='Anshul')

###Consume the Service Document - describe what are the entities part of my service
http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/CatalogService

###Metadat document of the odata service - $metadata
http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/CatalogService/$metadata

###Read my all Employee Data - Select * from Emp
http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/CatalogService/EmployeeSet
Authorization: Basic anubhav:Welcome1
### REad onlly the relevent fields from all employess - select id, nameFirst, nameLast, sex, email from Employeess
http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/CatalogService/EmployeeSet?$select=ID,nameFirst,nameLast,sex,email

### total count of employee record - $count
http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/CatalogService/EmployeeSet/$count

### Pagination load data by chunk - $top and $skip
http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/CatalogService/EmployeeSet?$top=2&$skip=2

### using ID
http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/CatalogService/EmployeeSet(ID='02BD2137-0890-1EEA-A6C2-BB55C198A7FB')
Authorization: Basic anubhav:Welcome1

### How to filter the data based on condition 
### select emp from My Bank of San Francisco
###eq nq, ge ,le, lt, gt
http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/CatalogService/EmployeeSet?$filter=bankName eq 'My Bank of San Francisco'&$top=2


###Example for v2
http://localhost:4004/odata/v2/CatalogService/EmployeeSet?$filter=bankName eq 'My Bank of San Francisco'

### Can we filter data based on Pattern match
http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/CatalogService/EmployeeSet?$filter=contains(nameFirst,'S')

###Sorting data - $orderby
http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/CatalogService/EmployeeSet?$orderby=salaryAmount desc

###Load the Purchase order data - all
http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/CatalogService/PurchaseOrderSet

###GEt Single Po data
http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/CatalogService/PurchaseOrderSet/74867AD200E41EDBA5D8B0C98DC46052

### GEt item data for this purchase order
http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/CatalogService/PurchaseOrderSet/74867AD200E41EDBA5D8B0C98DC28052/Items

###Load order header of a single order + its all item Together - $expand
http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/CatalogService/PurchaseOrderSet/74867AD200E41EDBA5D8B0C98DC46052?$expand=Items

###Using Cds view we do lazy loading
http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/CDSService/ProductSet/74867AD200E41EDBA5D8B06B26EBE052?$expand=To_Items

### Using Odata v4 allow filtering of child data also that was not there in v2
http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/CDSService/ProductSet/74867AD200E41EDBA5D8B06B26EBE052?$expand=To_Items($filter=TaxAmount le 500)

###Create operation to insert data into database


POST http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/CatalogService/EmployeeSet
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nameFirst": "Christiano",
  "nameMiddle": "null",
  "nameLast": "Babu",
  "nameInitials": null,
  "sex": "M",
  "language": "E",
  "phoneNumber": null,
  "email": "chrisian678@sap.com",
  "loginName": "CRFC",
  "Currency_code": "USD",
  "salaryAmount": 1000008,
  "accountNumber": "4125772788",
  "bankId": "12100",
  "bankName": "City Bank"
}

###change Data - update - copy the id created in last call 
PATCH http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/CatalogService/EmployeeSet/02BD2137-0890-1EEA-A6C2-BB55C198A7FB
Authorization: Basic anubhav:Welcome1
Content-Type: application/json 

{
    "salaryAmount": "19000"
}

### Delete the data from db
DELETE http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/CatalogService/EmployeeSet/02BD2137-0890-1EEA-A6C2-BB55C197C7FB

